edge_types.INHERITANCE_EDGE_TYPES existed and two consumers used it.
Six others each answered "is this an inheritance edge?" their own way and
disagreed: cli.py kept a complete hand-rolled copy, a second cli.py site
and _transitive_bases.py read ("extends", "implements"), inherited_calls
read ("extends", "implements", "includes"), and type_hierarchy branched
